  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d21438f07bf2e8446b0a1da7bf64f675, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day17
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dayNumber: 17
  storyText: "A small storm rolled in last night. Rain hammering the roof, wind howling
    through the cracks in the windows. We haven't seen the cats in a while. Not the
    fat orange one. Not the others. They're not on the canteen roof. Not under the
    trees. Not anywhere we can see. Maybe they found shelter. Maybe they didn't.
    The storm passed by morning, leaving everything wet and grey. The ducks are back,
    though. Shaking off water like nothing happened. We keep looking for the cats.
    Still nothing. We pretend it doesn't worry us. It does.\r"
